.TH IAD\-ENTRANCE 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
entrance \- Slides content in from offset (pixels) to its place on mount, optionally with a fading scrim over the whole layer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
entrance(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, offset: Vector)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Slides \fBcontent\fR in from \fBoffset\fR (pixels) to its place on mount, optionally with a fading scrim over the whole layer. Dialogs and sheets use the sheet spring (damping ratio 0.8, mass 1, stiffness 400); toasts use 300ms \fBADW_EASE\fR.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B entrance(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, offset: Vector)
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.scrim(radius: f32)
Draws a scrim (rounded to \fBradius\fR) behind the content that fades in with it.
.TP
.B \&.spec(spec: Spec)
.TP
.B \&.trigger(t: Trigger)
Which trigger this entrance is: \fBTrigger::Dialog\fR (default), \fBSheet\fR or \fBToast\fR. Its \fB[motion]\fR setting (or reduced motion) can turn the animation off.
